  "body": "## What changed\n\nEvery issue branch appended to the end of `RECOMMENDED.md`, so each merge re-conflicted every other open PR on that file. Now:\n\n- A PR records its decisions in its own file, `docs/decisions/<issue>-<slug>.md`, in the same format (`docs/decisions/README.md`). Issue branches never edit `RECOMMENDED.md`.\n- At the cut, `scripts/collect-decisions.ps1 -Version X.Y.Z` (or `collect-decisions.sh`) appends every decision file, in issue-number order, to `RECOMMENDED.md` under a `## vX.Y.Z` heading, and removes them. AGENTS.md release step 2 runs it in the docs commit.\n- AGENTS.md's 'Every recommendation is recorded', the Issue Law intro and step 1's merge note are updated to match.\n\n## Readings\n\nBoth scripts were smoke-tested: with no files they're a no-op, and with files 9/12/100 they come out in order 9, 12, 100, the files are removed and README.md is kept. RECOMMENDED.md was restored after the test.\n\nOpen PRs that already append to RECOMMENDED.md keep merging main with both sides kept until they land; only new work uses the new files.\n\nChangelog: none\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
